Tariff Pressures & Supply Chain Volatility: Recent U.S. tariffs on steel, aluminum, and imports from China, Mexico, and Canada have disproportionately impacted small businesses. Many face rising costs, canceled orders, and margin compression, making it harder to scale competitively.
Capital & Infrastructure Gaps: Competing with giants like Home Depot or Lowe’s requires significant investment in logistics, warehousing, and marketing. Without access to capital or government support, small firms may struggle to match the scale and efficiency of incumbents.
Brand Recognition & Consumer Trust: Large hardware brands benefit from decades of brand equity and customer loyalty. Overcoming this requires not just superior products, but also compelling narratives and transparent documentation—something you’ve already begun embedding in your alliance-safe storefronts and artifact protocols.
